C  controls (noise-free unless stated)
==============================================================================================================
  [FAIL] C1 CONTROL: a noise-free POINT-MASS mock (no pressure, no smearing) is recovered by the PM estimator (|dLambda| < 2e-3 dex)
         measured: flat +4.6e-01, rival (vs log10 E(z_med)) +5.5e-01 dex -- the rival's per-disc E(z_i) spread makes the rival residual non-zero by construction; flat is the exact test
  [FAIL] C1b CONTROL: a noise-free DISC mock with the declared shape (mu 0.67, R_gas 2 R_d) is recovered by the DS estimator (|dLambda| < 2e-3 dex)
         measured: flat +6.1e-01 dex; the PM estimator on the same mock gives +1.500 (edge True)
  [FAIL] C2 CONTROL: a pure-Newtonian point-mass mock gives s = -1, y -> infinity, i.e. only an UPPER limit on a0: the PM stack sits at the grid's lower edge (Lambda <= -1.49)
         measured: Lambda_hat -0.690, edge False
  reported: a pure-Newtonian DISC mock (declared shape) -> DS Lambda_hat -0.574 (edge False); PM Lambda_hat +0.359 (edge False): the point-mass form reads a spurious finite a0 off a Newtonian disc

